# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored at every level; this file is
# tracked and must never contain a real value.
#
# EITHER of these satisfies the boot gate -- they are what `agent-service-spec`
# publishes as `credential_sources`. The FIRST non-empty one wins.
#
# **THE APP-SERVER DOES NOT READ THEM.** Measured 2026-08-08: exporting a key
# into its process leaves `account()` null and every turn comes back
# `401 Missing bearer or basic authentication in header`. The only way in is
# `login_api_key()`, which THIS SERVICE performs at session open using whichever
# of these is set. So they are where the service reads a key from, not a
# mechanism the SDK honours -- see docs/sdk-assessment.md section 12.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# CODEX_API_KEY=

# A ROUTE THIS GATE CANNOT SEE. `login_api_key()` writes the key into the
# app-server's auth store under CODEX_HOME, so a mounted CODEX_HOME carrying a
# login from an earlier run -- or a ChatGPT login performed by hand -- is
# already authenticated with no variable set. Such a deployment must start with:
# AGENT_SERVICE_REQUIRE_CREDENTIALS=false

# Where the app-server keeps its SQLite state, installation id, auth store and
# unpacked skills -- 65 files on first start. IT MUST EXIST; the app-server will
# not create it. Mount this to keep threads across a container restart.
# AGENT_SERVICE_CODEX_HOME=./codex-home
